1 NAME Daniel /Lewin/
2 GIVN Daniel
2 _MARNM Lewin
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 14 MAR 1901
2 PLAC Pinne
2 ADDR
3 CITY Posen | Poznań
3 STAE Greater Poland Voivodeship
3 CTRY Germany now Poland
1 DEAT
2 DATE 11 SEP 1997
2 ADDR
3 CITY Montreal
3 STAE Quebec
3 CTRY Canada
1 OCCU Rabbi
1 TITL Rabbi
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.newspapers.com/article/the-gazette-obituary-for-daniel-lewin/78201362/
2 CONT
2 CONT Yeshiva University collection note: Articles by and letters to Rabbi Daniel Lewin, including biographical material about him. Articles and essays by Michael Fraenkel, some with the author's autograph, including some offprints from
2 CONC  "Der Oberschlesiers": Monatsschrift fur das Heimat. Kulturleben, published between 1930 and 1934. Some of Lewin's articles are in newspapers, some are published in periodicals, and some are typescripts. Fraenkel's articles are in
2 CONC  booklets. Also included are typescript inventories of these items. There is also a photocopy of a letter from Dr. Samuel Belkin, New York, to Daniel Lewin, London, of September 13, 1946 expressing an interest in acquiring Louis L
2 CONC ewin's collection for Yeshiva University. A letter from Isaac Lewin, New York, to Daniel Lewin, May 11, 1948, confirms the receipt of trunks of the Louis Lewin collection at Yeshiva University. A catalog of Swann Auction Galleries
2 CONC  pertains to an auction to be held on February 15, 1951 where books from Louis Lewin's library were on sale. Some of the items are photocopies of articles by Louis Lewin and a handwritten eulogy for him by Rabbi Dr. M. Kahn. Also 
2 CONC included is a copy of The Jewish herald: organ of the new Zionist organization of Southern Africa, Johannesburg, S.A., January 24, 1941. Lewin Collection. Gift of Mrs. Eva Lewis.
2 CONT
2 CONT In Hebrew, German, and English.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note that Daniel Lewin's mother was the daughter of Rabbi Michael Fraenkel. Note also that Daniel Lewin's father was Rabbi Louis Lewin. 
