1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Bergman, Shirley Claire 92 Aug. 15, 1919 Oct. 09, 2011 Shirley Claire (nee Savinar) Bergman died Oct. 9, 2011. She was 92. A native and lifelong resident of Portland, Shirley was born Aug. 15, 1919, to Jacob W. and
2 CONC  Bessie Abrams Savinar. Her girlhood home stood at the corner of Northeast 21st Avenue and Weidler Street. She was in the first class to attend Irvington Elementary School and graduated from U.S. Grant High School in June 1938. Sh
2 CONC e was most proud of the continuation of her studies, which culminated in her graduation from Portland State University with a bachelor's degree in the fall of 1996, at age 77. Shirley married Leo M. Bergman, the late founder and p
2 CONC resident of Paint Specialties, Inc., Jan. 16, 1943. They lived almost their entire married life in Portland's Alameda neighborhood. An inveterate walker, Shirley thought nothing of hiking from there to the Lloyd Center and back in
2 CONC  an after-noon. She also loved her cats, her books and the quiet tranquility of her verdant backyard. She worked for many years as a teacher's aide-with special emphasis on reading-first at the Fruit and Flower Day Nursery and lat
2 CONC er at Irivington, Rose City Park and numerous other elementary schools. Mrs. Bergman is survived by her son, Michael, of Olympia, Wash.; daughter, Jill Strasser of Portland; and five grandchildren. Memorial gifts may be made to th
2 CONC e Friends of the Multnomah County Library or the Oregon Humane Society. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Published in The Oregonian on Oct. 11, 2011
