1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT 13 August 1833 Van Diemen's Advertiser, page 2. Ship News.
2 CONT August 11. The ship Thomas, 329 tons, Captain Henley, from Leith and the Cape of Good Hope, with a general cargo. 
2 CONT and 150 mechanics, including their wives and children. five children born during the voyage. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret was 18 years old and about 3 month pregnant when she married 26 year old James Cairns in Hobart, witnesses to the wedding ceremony was her 21 year old brother James and their 24 year old sister Mrs Mary Rose. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 1850 her husband James Cairns was witness at Margaret's brother,   James Hay Kittelty marriage in Hobart to Susan Player. 
2 CONT
2 CONT lived south of Geeveston, at or near Cairns Bay
2 CONT
2 CONT Inquest - Fire dwelling house of Margaret Cairns - 13 June 1884 SC195/1/64 No 8838 1884 
2 CONT Tasmania Archives
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Chronic kidney infection, Diarrhoea, Syncope, aged 59 years
