1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Charlotte arrived in Tasmania aboard the "Thomas" in Aug 1833 with her parents. Although she was born in Scotland, she was baptised in Tasmania on 31 Aug 1833. She was buried 25 Feb 1902 in the Ballarat New Cemeter
2 CONC y.
2 CONT
2 CONT Info states that Charlotte was aged 21 at the time of their marriage; Source:  http://daltondata.0pi.com/tasmania.html
2 CONT
2 CONT William and Charlotte both arrived in Ballarat, Victoria, Australia, from Tasmania, around 1850 - after the birth of second son, Henry.
2 CONT
2 CONT *The following from Gail Stapleton via email:
2 CONT
2 CONT Ballarat New Cemetery
2 CONT
2 CONT Church of England, COFEC, 3, 46
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruth Florence Ebsworthy aged 12 days 6/10/1902, Murphy St, Ballarat, grand daughter of Charlotte & John.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Ebsworthy aged 66 Engine Driver 23/4/1891 Clayton St Ballarat, husband of Charlotte
2 CONT
2 CONT Charlotte Ebsworthy aged 70 Widow 25/2/1902 Ballarat Hospital, wife of Richard John Ebsworthy
2 CONT
2 CONT no headstone on record
2 CONT
2 CONT *Wednesday 26th February 1902
2 CONT
2 CONT The Ballarat Courier
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary
2 CONT
2 CONT Service by Archdeacon Tucker
2 CONT
2 CONT 4 22 Mar 2008
2 CONT
2 CONT Undertaker Thos Wellington
2 CONT
2 CONT Pall bearers G Maloney, W Maynard, P Magee, V Dalton
2 CONT
2 CONT Coffin bearers J Radford, W Williams, H Kettelty, W Barrett
2 CONT
2 CONT *Baptism: 31 Aug 1833, 32/4837 Charlotte Burnett Kettlety, parents Anne & Solomon Kettlety, Hobart
2 CONT
2 CONT Town, Tasmania, Australia
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: 25 Feb 1902, Ballarat New Cemetery COFEC, 3, 46
2 CONT
2 CONT Cemetery Record: 1902, Charlotte Ebsworthy aged 70 Widow
2 CONT
2 CONT Death Cert No: 1902, 268, 16 years in Tasmania, 50 years in Victoria
2 CONT
2 CONT Emigrated: 26 Aug 1833, Ship Thomas, aged 5 years
2 CONT
2 CONT Medical Information: Died in Hospital in Ballarat
2 CONT
2 CONT Residence: Bet. 1868 - 1902, Ballarat
