1 NAME Dorothy /Sorem/
2 GIVN Dorothy
2 SURN Sorem
2 _MARNM Munz
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 14 SEP 1932
2 ADDR
3 CITY San Francisco
3 STAE California
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 19 NOV 2003
2 ADDR
3 CITY Eugene
3 STAE Oregon
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Dorothy Munz 
2 CONT
2 CONT Dorothy Munz of Eugene died Nov. 19 of cancer. She was 71. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Munz was born Sept. 14, 1932, in San Francisco and was adopted by Clifford and Edith Sorem. She married Frederick Munz in Eureka, Calif., on July 24, 1954. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She grew up in the California cities of Ferndale and Arcata. She graduated from Pomona College, where she majored in music. She moved to Eugene in 1959 and performed solo and ensemble piano recitals. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She worked as a private piano teacher and she was an adjudicator for the Oregon Music Teachers Association. She was the first editor of the journal, The Oregon Musician. She also co-wrote and published two books of piano pedagogy.
2 CONC
2 CONT
2 CONT She enjoyed traveling, the outdoors, hiking, camping, backpacking and bird-watching. She especially enjoyed visiting with her family and friends during the last days of her illness. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She will be remembered as an outgoing person who studied French, German and Italian so she could converse with the people she met on her travels. She belonged to a close-knit and loyal group of friends who played bridge, conversed
2 CONC  and lunched together for more than 30 years. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include her husband; two daughters, Sara Munz of Portland and Alice Cura of California; a son, Carl of Portland; and one grandchild. 
2 CONT
2 CONT At her request, no service is planned. Poole-Larsen Funeral Home in Eugene is in charge of arrangements. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: https://www.thefreelibrary.com/OBITUARIES.-a0112803769
