1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Based on the interview of his brother Jacques and the second page of Leo's passenger manifest, The Bergman family lived in  Vienna, Austria. They lived in the second district of Vienna, near the Nordwestbahnhof. Le
2 CONC o was born at home on Blumauergasse 20. From 8 Jun 1921 – 2 May 1940, they lived at Alliiertenstraße 6/9.
2 CONT
2 CONT From his petition for naturalization: Leo Bergmann, Gender:	Male, Petition Age:	23, Record Type:Petition, Birth Date:	7 Aug 1918, Birth Place:	Vienna, Austria. On his passenger manifest, next of kin is listed as I. Bergman at 6 Eb
2 CONC arta Str. Vienna.  Leo left Vienna and traveled to Le Havre, France, where he sailed on the Britannic to New York, Arrival Date: 23 Oct 1938, Arrival Place: New York, New York. He lived for awhile in Connecticut. When he enroled i
2 CONC n the army, Residence Place: Portland, Oregon, Petition Date:12 Jun 1942, Petition Place:Oregon, USA. From Leo's WWII Army Enlistment: Enlistment Date:	5 Aug 1941, Enlistment State:Connecticut, Enlistment City: Hartford, Branch: B
2 CONC ranch Immaterial - Warrant Officers, USA, Branch Code:	Branch Immaterial - Warrant Officers, USA, Grade: Private, Grade Code: Private, Term of Enlistment: Enlistment for Hawaiian Department, Component:Selectees (Enlisted Men) Sour
2 CONC ce: Civil Life, Education: 4 years of college, Civil Occupation:Pressmen and plate printers, printing, Marital status: Single, without dependents, Height: 70 in, Weight: 195 lbs. Enlistment Date 1: 5 Aug 1941, Release Date 1: 9 Se
2 CONC p 1945. He served with 1633rd Engineer Photomapping Platoon and was listed on the Personnel List, November 1943 - November 1945.
