2 NOTE Hi Ellen,
3 CONT     I'd love to see you.  I'm in Israel about twice a year....and will be there from July 1st to August 3rd.  I'm co-chair of one of the Partnerships of the Sochnut. I'm comin in February to co-chair a steering committee meeting b
3 CONC ut am just staying for ten days so I can go visit grandsons in Connecticut a week later and help out my daughter.  I LOVE being a savta!
3 CONT  I'm delighted that I inspired you.  On Sunday I connected with part of my mom's family (most of which died in the Holocaust).  There are in Israel....and will see them again this summer.  They came in 1991 from White Russia.  And
3 CONC  the cousin my mom's age has a great nepher on her husband's side in Tel Aviv who has added a lot to the family history.  Warm regards to Bobbee too.
2 NOTE Of course I know who you are!  Your pictures inspired me to post these.  On December 20 we had the unveiling of my father's headstone here in Jerusalem, the day before my mother's 6th yartzheit.  Bobbee was coming in for the yartz
3 CONC heit, so we decided to go ahead with the unveiling during her trip as well. It's the norm to erect the matzeivah quickly here, not waiting a year as is often the case in the States.
3 CONT  I am really glad that you remember my parents that way; I have no doubt that it is exactly as they would want to be remembered.  Come visit us here in Jerusalem.
