2 CONT The Jew in South Africa: A record of what individual Jews are doing in various spheres of the country’s life. Who’s Who.  Edited Rabbi Maurice Konvisser and Dora Sowden.  Century Publishing 1945. page 297:  Beinasowitz, Abraham Le
2 CONC ib  Woollen Merchant, Commissioner of Oaths. Born in Poswohl Lithuania in 1876. Educated in Riga. Married in 1902 to Sarah Meyer: has five children. Ardent Communal Worker: Chairman Poswohl Hebrew Congregation, 1906-1913; Treasure
2 CONC r of same, 1913-1929; Committee Member of the Jjewish Burial and Helping Hand Society, 1917-1927; Committee Member, Jewish Aged Home for several years. Takes part in all Zionist effort. Postal Address: P.O.Box 4359 Johannesburg. 
