1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sudden Death.  On Friday, at the Black Ball Hotel, Ballarat, Dr Clendinning, held an inquest on the body of John Rose, whose death, according to the evidence adduced, and the verdict of the jury, took place in his 
2 CONC own house.  Urquhart street, Ballarat West, and arose from natural causes, being caused by syncope, brought on by disease of the heart.  The deceased who was fifty three years of age a stonemason by trade, and a native of Wiltshir
2 CONC e, had been ailing for some time, and died suddenly on the evening of Thursday. 
