1 NAME Elizabeth /Vickers nee Rose/
2 GIVN Elizabeth
2 _MARNM Vickers nee Rose
1 SEX F
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Book - Women of the Diggings Ballarat 1854 by Dorothy Wickham
2 CONT Elizabeth Rose
2 CONT Elizabeth was born at Hobart Town, Tasmania on 11 January 1840. She arrived in Geelong, Victoria around 1853.  She lived in a tent at Ballarat during the Eureka Stockade Riots, the tent being situated between the soldiers camp and
2 CONC  that of the miners.  She married merchant Isaac Vickers on 23 November 1861.  They lived at Colac, Ballarat, Sebastopol, Bendigo for forty years and Coburg.  Elizabeth died on 22 September 1916 and was buried in the Boroondara Ce
2 CONC metery, Kew. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 28 Sept 1916
2 CONT Vickers On the 22nd September (suddenly), at the residence of her nephew, Mr Percival G Lennox, Coburg of broncho pneumonia, Elizabeth, wife of the late Isaac Vickers, formerly of Bendigo and loved mother of Daisy,  Mrs Vibert, He
2 CONC rbert T, and Ernest L, in her 77th year, private interment.
2 CONT "Blessed are the dead which die in the Lord" 
2 CONT
2 CONT 29 Sept 1916
2 CONT Western Mail, Perth
2 CONT Vickers On September 22 1916, passed away peacefully at Coburg, Victoria.  Elizabeth, widow of the late Isaac Vickers, Bendigo, Beloved mother of Mrs P H Vibert and E L Vickers, Subiaco, and Herbert T and Daisie Vickers, Melbourne
2 CONC , aged 76 years. For ever with the Lord. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 6 Oct 1916
2 CONT The Herald Melbourne.
2 CONT Probate of Will of Elizabeth Vickers, late of Suffolk Road, Coburg, formerly 56 Old Violet St, Bendigo, Widow, deceased be granted to Herbert Theodore Vickers of "Weardale" 13 Dixon St, Malvern, Public Servant, being the executor 
2 CONC appointed by the said Will.  
2 CONT
2 CONT This is the last Will and Testament of me 
2 CONT Elizabeth Vickers of Rosebourne 56 Old Violet Street, Bendigo I give devise and bequeath unto my daughter Sarah Elizabeth 
2 CONT Frances (Daisy) after the payment of all my just debts funeral and testamentary expenses all my real and personal estate. 
