1 NOTE {geni:about_me} James Cairns, Convicted at Glasgow, Court of Justiciary on 10 Sept 1835, Sentence 7 years
2 CONT
2 CONT Departure: 12 Jul 1836, Transported from UK age 18 to Tasmania, Van Diemen's Land
2 CONT
2 CONT  12 Nov 1836, Arrived in Tas. aboard Lady Nugent
2 CONT
2 CONT  08 Jan 1836, Trial & conviction for theft of watch Glasgow, Strathcylde, Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT Occupation: Sailor prior to transportation
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr Leach once for Theft 2 months, 3 times ? for Misbehaviour & Vagrancy 2 months each time, Single, Surgeon's report, behaves very well.
2 CONT
2 CONT July 23 1841 Misconduct in using ? Language  July 30 1841 Misconduct in being in a Public house  after hours  & unpresenting at his authorized place of residence 48 hours hard labor 
2 CONT
2 CONT November 30 1841 ? Misconduct in ? and being in town without reporting himself 2 months hard labour 
2 CONT
2 CONT To leave Hobart
2 CONT
2 CONT February 1 1842 Misconduct 14 days hard labour 
2 CONT
2 CONT Then to leave Hobart Town 
2 CONT
2 CONT Free Certificate 282 1843 
