1 NOTE {geni:about_me} George Dalton was responsible for painting at Sheldricks new Brewery published in the Warrnambool Standard 7th October 1892.
2 CONT
2 CONT A cutting from a local newspaper.  By the death of George William Dalton which occurred recently another link with the early days of Warrnambool has been severed.
2 CONT
2 CONT The late gentleman was a resident of the city for over 50 years, and carried on business as a house painter and decorator.
2 CONT
2 CONT For many years he held the position of secretary of the local Foresters' Court and was intimately associated with the early history of the friendly societies Park.  He was also captain of the local Fire Brigade.  While anything th
2 CONC at had to be done for the advancement of the town gained his ever ready suppport.  All branches of athletic sport had his patronage, and he was himself a very fine gymnast, boxer and pole vaulter.  He had reached the age of 81 yea
2 CONC rs at the time of his death and leaves a grown up family of 10 sons and daughters to mourn their loss.  His wife predeceased him some years ago.
2 CONT
2 CONT
