1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Letter written by Minnie in New Zealand & sent to Minnie's daughter Vera Jones in Ballarat, Australia
2 CONT
2 CONT Reefton 4th 6th 1946 (4th June)
2 CONT
2 CONT To my Darling Daughter,
2 CONT
2 CONT Well my Dear you will never know how thrilled I was to recieve your dear letter, & I know you were all well & oh how delighted I was to see you dear face & the little ones thank you very much dear & we all thought they were lovely
2 CONC  & you look so nice in your little 
2 CONT
2 CONT frock dress & your little 
2 CONT
2 CONT ? lovely did you make them dear.
2 CONT
2 CONT Della has just came for us to go for a walk it is such a lovely day but I said I would rather have a little chat to you I would have been over to see you & the Family but they say you would not get back for two years so that upset
2 CONC  the apple cart I will be 84 in August next but I still get about & go to the pictures every Saturday night Fred 
2 CONT
2 CONT Grace  (her daughter & son in law)  & I go every Saturday night & any night there is a good one on I am going to the Band ?
2 CONT
2 CONT I might with Mr Hunt I go every Wenesday afternoon to the  Croaky clubs 
2 CONT
2 CONT afternoon 500 so you see your old mum is a giddy old spark I am very pleased to say every one is well only Gracie's Vie's feet trouble her a lot & her right hand it is 
2 CONT
2 CONT nutritus I think she was in the hospital for a fortnight she has a miscarrage her oldest boy Grant is in bed with a sore throat & he has had a lot of boils on his legs Alf wife is having another little one next month that will be 
2 CONC four.  Jack as two & Gracie's Vie two Alf's little boy Peter goes to school they have just got over the measels  
2 CONT
2 CONT Fred has the house finished all but putting the fence up & that wont take long it is a credit to him the way he has
2 CONT
2 CONT don it for it looks very nice & Grace will have lawns & gardens around the  ?
2 CONT
2 CONT I am enclosing Myrtle (her daughter Charlotte Myrtle Sharp nee Magee)  letter to you as I thought you would like to read it & your poho to look at but that has to come back Myrt & Vie was down for five weeks as Myrtle does not kee
2 CONC p very good health & Vie husband was killed at the war on a 
2 CONT
2 CONT rout Vie gets 7 a week pension I hope you wrote to dear Aunty Charlotte  (is she referring to her sister Charlotte Dalton who lives in Victoria, Australia) as she does love you Vera oh how I would love to see her I just feel like 
2 CONC flying over to see you all Mrs George Crossman died a few months ago & Mrs Cook & did I tell you old Mrs Wicken & Dora Farrells mother died Dora is married & got one little boy all my old friends have died or gone away I am on my 
2 CONC only lonely now I was out at the Cemetery last week & put a few flowers on poor Dad's (she must be referring to her husband James Magee, who died 1944)  oh how I do miss him I got a letter from Emma that is Gill Mainard (Gill is M
2 CONC innie's nephew) wife in Perth & sent Emma & Myrtle so she tells me to put more water in it the smell of it is enough it is awfull the way the girls drink & smoke these days my word dear little Audrey (Audrey Jones, Minnie's grand 
2 CONC daughter)  must be a big girl & a very cleaver girl too just fancy her working in a shop good luck dear Audrey & God bless you she must be lovely company for you dear Vera oh how I wish you were over here you could make your fortu
2 CONC ne as there is only 
2 CONT
2 CONT ?
2 CONT
2 CONT here now one cannot get a dress made now we went to see 25 young girls presented & the 
2 CONT
2 CONT Cuth ? last friday night & it was lovely there was 600 there the girls also & the bogues were beautifull it was only ? to look on & 10/6 to dance so me did not dance well my dears
2 CONT
2 CONT as it is nearly tea time I must lay the table 
2 CONT
2 CONT so will say ta ta & lots of love from 
2 CONT
2 CONT Your ever loving Old mum
2 CONT
2 CONT God bless XXXXX
2 CONT
2 CONT my love to the girls & family & a big hug for my great son-in-laws
2 CONT
2 CONT Buried Plot 576 Reefton Cemetery New Zealand
