1 NOTE {geni:about_me} National Advocate Bathurst NSW Tue 10 Oct 1916
2 CONT Meeting at Ballarat.  Labor Anti-Conscriptionist in Majority
2 CONT Monday A non-conscription meeting was held at the Alfred Hall, Ballarat, under the auspices of the Political Labor Council.  Mr W A Dalton president of Ballarat branch occupied the chair.  There was a crowded attendance, estimated
2 CONC  at 3000 people including many ladies. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1916 McCallum, Directory
2 CONT Walter A Dalton; b Ball (on site of St. Paul's
2 CONT Churchyard), 1864; son. of W H Dalton (fdtn. mbr. & officer of St. Paul's Church. of England; one of earliest mbrs. Ball. Fire Brigade, Pioneer Lodge, I.O.O.F.; previous to which was master mariner); educ. St. Paul's S.S. served i
2 CONC n Vol. Rifle Rangers & 3rd Batt. Inf.; pres. Ball. E. electoral cl. of P.L.C.; pres. Ball. P.L.C.; mbr. Eureka Stockade Memorial Park Commitee; spent some years in N.Z.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Ballarat Star Wed 2 May 1917 Page 8
2 CONT Labor Meetings.  Labor election meetings to night at 8 o'clock, will be addressed at the corner of Lane and Humffray streets, Messrs W A Dalton and R. Whibrick will speak.
2 CONT Thursday night at 8 o'clock Messrs W A Dalton and J Meehan at Mount Clear (Horwoods')  
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The Ballarat Star Thurs 7 Oct  1920 Page 2
2 CONT Ballarat East 
2 CONT Mr W Dalton's Candidature
2 CONT There was a fair attendance at the Ballarat East Library Hall last night, when Mr W Dalton, who is opposing the Hon. R McGregor MLA, in the Labor interests. for the Ballarat seat in the Legislative Assembly, formally opened his ca
2 CONC mpaign. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr Dalton who was well received, remarked that it was an honor to be the selected candidate for Labor. 
