1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From ''[http://www.cba.cobar.org/tcl/tcl_articles.cfm?articleid=599 The Colorado Lawyer]'':
2 CONT
2 CONT > Colorado native and long-time Denver attorney '''David R. Gorsuch''' passed away on April 17, 2001. He was 65. Gorsuch was born in Denver. He attended the University of Colorado, Boulder, graduating from the School of Law in 196
2 CONC 4. He was admitted to the Colorado Bar that same year and became a member of the CBA in 1965. He practiced law at the Denver firm of Gorsuch Kirgis LLC, retiring as senior and managing partner in 1995. Gorsuch was president of Den
2 CONC ver Kiwanis Club. He served on the board of directors at St. Joseph Hospital, Emily Griffith School for Boys, and Emily Griffith Foundation. Survivors include his wife, Peggy, several children and stepchildren, and one grandchild.
2 CONC  Memorial contributions may be made to the Emily Griffith Center Foundation, 8745 W. 14th Ave., Suite 230, Lakewood, CO 80215.
2 CONT
2 CONT From [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anne_Gorsuch_Burford Wikipedia]:
2 CONT
2 CONT > "[Politician and attorney Anne McGill] married '''David Gorsuch''' after finishing law school. The couple had two sons, J.J. and Neil, and a daughter (Stephanie).  Neil Gorsuch is a Federal court judge for United States Court of
2 CONC  Appeals for the Tenth Circuit.
2 CONT
2 CONT > Anne and David Gorsuch divorced in 1982..."
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
