2 CONT
2 CONT Moritz was a fur merchant who left Germany for Canada in 1884.  He became a naturalized Canadian in 1887.  In 1888, Moritz was the sole heir of his older brother Jacob in British Columbia.  Jacob had died in a gale on his schooner
2 CONC  “Active” on  01 Apr 1887. Moritz partnered a fur dealer and taxidermy company with W. Lindley at 24 Government St. in Victoria, B.C.  According to the paper The British Colonist, 07 Feb 1903, Moritz retired from that firm on 31 J
2 CONC an 1903.  The widowed Moritz moved his family to Seattle in late 1903. Ellis Island records from the ship Cuxhaven, 08 Sep 1903, show that Moritz lived at that time at 171 Pandora St. in Victoria, British Columbia.  Ellis Island r
2 CONC ecords from the ship Bremen, 09 May 1905, show that Moritz was headed to Seattle, WA, where he owned his own home at 1811 1st Street. Moritz established the Hudson Bay Fur Company branch in Seattle. He had founded this company in 
2 CONC 1900; its name was changed to the Alaska Fur Company in 1942.
