1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Carolyn Frances Savinar Selling ’44
2 CONT A picture of Carolyn Savinar Selling
2 CONT Carolyn Frances Savinar Selling ’44, May 4, 2005, in Portland. Carolyn attended Reed for three years, and earned a BA in social welfare from UC Berkeley in 1944. She married John L. Selling ’37 in 1945; they had three children, an
2 CONC d later divorced. Carolyn completed a master’s in social work from Portland State University in 1965. She worked as executive director of Social Work Careers in Oregon, and as program consultant and field instructor at Albertina K
2 CONC err Homes for nearly 25 years, retiring in 1989. She was also on the board of directors for Albertina Kerr Centers and Planned Parenthood, was a member of the Citizens Review Board, Oregon chapter president of the National Associa
2 CONC tion of Social Work, and a board member of the Reed alumni association. Survivors include her daughter and sons, and two grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.reed.edu/reed-magazine/in-memoriam/obituaries/august2005/carolyn-frances-savinar-selling-1944.html Appeared in Reed magazine: August 2005]
2 CONT
