1 TITL Rabbi
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Paid Notice: Deaths  POPLACK, RABBI ALVIN MYRON Published: January 1, 2012
2 CONT
2 CONT POPLACK--Rabbi Alvin Myron, 91, died on December 24, 2011 with his three children by his side. He was predeceased by 66 days by his wife of 66 years, the former Rosalind Schachter. Son of Rabbi Alter and Genia Trakeniski Poplack, 
2 CONC he was ordained at Rabbinical Seminary Chaim Berlin (New York) in 1944. Rabbi Poplack held a Masters from Yeshiva University, and a PhD from Jewish Teachers Seminary. During WWII he served as civilian chaplain in the USO Jewish We
2 CONC lfare Board. He held pulpits in Detroit, MI, Medford, MA, and Lebanon, PA before becoming Rabbi (1956) and Rabbi Emeritus (1986) of the Bellerose Jewish Center (New York). He served as President of the Queens Council for Soviet Je
2 CONC wry, and Secretary of the New York Board of Rabbis. As Senior Chaplain, Rabbi Poplack spearheaded the reconstruction of the International Synagogue at JFK Airport, and was spiritual leader to the JFK community and travelers from a
2 CONC ll over the world. He was the author of Carved In Granite: Holocaust Memorials in Metropolitan New York Jewish Cemeteries (2003), a work read and endorsed by leading Holocaust scholars. He is profoundly missed by his loving childr
2 CONC en, grandchildren, great-grandchildren, and by family, friends, colleagues, former congregants and the countless people whose lives he touched.
