1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Baynash , Jack Beinashowitz, M.D. (Univ . Edin.) , 1932, M.R.C.P (Edin.), 1933. and practiced as Dr Jack Baynash. He served as doctor in the Armed Forces in WWII and was stationed at a field hospital in Kenya. 28 H
2 CONC e married Esther Jacobs in Mombasa, Kenya in March 1944. He returned to South Africa and  subsequently worked at the Heights (Voortrekker Hoogte, Pretoria).  He specialised as a physician and worked as  senior physician at the Joh
2 CONC annesburg General Hospital.   He died in London in 1953, at the age of 50 years. He was buried in the Westpark Cemetery Johannesburg. The  Jack Baynash Prize in Medicine is awarded  at the University of the Witwatersrand to medica
2 CONC l students for the standard of work as reflected in clinical clerking in the fourth and fifth years of study.  
