1 NAME William Leslie /Kittelty/
2 GIVN William Leslie
2 SURN Kittelty
2 _MARNM Kittelty
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 4 OCT 1886
2 ADDR
3 CITY Greymouth
3 STAE South Island
3 CTRY New Zealand
1 BURI
2 DATE AFT 8 AUG 1915
2 PLAC Chunuk Bair New Zealand Memorial
2 ADDR
3 ADR1 [Panel 10.]
3 CITY Eceabat İlçesi
3 STAE Çanakkale
3 CTRY Türkiye
1 DEAT
2 DATE 8 AUG 1915
2 ADDR
3 CITY Gelibolu
3 STAE Çanakkale
3 CTRY Türkiye
1 OCCU Auckland Infantry Battalion
1 TITL Pte.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William Kittelty was the son of Esther Kittelty, of 76, Prospect Terrace, Mount Eden, Auckland, and the late William Kittelty. Native of Greymouth. Private in AIR, file number 12/25. Wounded 27 April 1915 in right 
2 CONC forearm and fingers during the Battle of the Landing, Kittelty spent 5 weeks in hospital before returning to the front. He was killed in the charge at the Pinnacle during the August Offensive. Kittelty's sister, 22/136 Eliza Jane 
2 CONC Kittelty, NZANS (on HS Maheno) also served in WW1.
2 CONT
