1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 5 March 1918, Powlett Express and Victorian State Coalfields Advertiser, Page 2
2 CONT
2 CONT Wedding Kittelty, Atcheson.
2 CONT An interesting wedding took place at the Presbyterian Church, Wonthaggi on Wednesday, February 24, when Mr W Kittelty, Poowong (son of the late James Kittelty, and Mrs Kittelty, formerly of Kilcunda), and Miss E Atcheson, of Outtr
2 CONC im, were married by Rev Mr Buntine, of Dandenong.  The bride who was given away by her uncle Mr G Atcheson, North Wonthaggi, was gowned in a handsome cream satin under dress, with cream silk over lace and wore the usual veil with 
2 CONC orange blossoms.  Miss McLean, Outtrim, attended as bridesmaid, in a pretty dress of white emboidered crepe-de-chine with white hat, trimmed with white roses and ribbon.  Mr D Munro was best man. 
2 CONT Mr Condy, organist, presided at the organ and played the wedding march. 
2 CONT The breakfast too place at Easton's Crystal palace and the usual toasts were honored.  The happy couple go honeymooning in Tasmania and will later reside at Poowong. The bride travelled in a blue serge costume, trimmed with blue s
2 CONC ilk and buttons, blue silk hat with large white plumes. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 18 Jan 1919 The Australian, Melbourne, Page 53
2 CONT Kittelty - Blair.  On the 24th December, in Melbourne, William B Kittelty, eldest son of Mrs S Kittelty, Poowong to Charlotte, youngest daughter of Mr Robert Blair, Hentone Lodge, South Shields, England. 
