1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The Argus, Melbourne, Tuesday 14 May 1935
2 CONT Notice is hereby given, that after the 
2 CONT expiration of fourteen days from the publication hereof application will be made to the Supreme Court of the State of Victoria, in its Probate jurisdiction, that Probate of the Will dated the sixth day of August 1928, of Alice 
2 CONT Louise Waite, late of Chapman street, Sunshine, in the State of Victoria, married woman, deceased, may be granted to John James Kittelty, of Chapman street, Sunshine aforesaid ammunition worker, one of the executors appointed by t
2 CONC he said will, leave being reserved to Catherine Sophia May Kittelty (in the said will called Catherine S M Kittelty), of Chapman street, Sunshine aforesaid, married woman, the other executor named in the said will 
2 CONT  to come in and prove the same. Dated the 13th day of May, 1935.  Martin & Martin, 314 Collins street, Melbourne
