1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sunshine Advocate Friday 7th Febrary 1936
2 CONT Wedding
2 CONT Murray - Kittelty
2 CONT On Saturday last, February 1, the Presbyterian Church, Sunshine, was the scene of a picturesque wedding, when Jean, only daughter of Mrs F Murray and the late Mr Murray, of 169 Morris Street, Sunshine, was joined in matrimony to J
2 CONC ack H Eldest son of Mr and Mrs Kittelty of Chapman Street, Sunshine. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The bride, who was given away by her uncle Mr Carruthers, of East Malvern, looked very charming in a frock of chenille georgette with a silver thread.  It was cut on simple lines, the bodice having a cowl neck caught with a spray 
2 CONC of orange blossom, long full sleeves, the skirt graduating to form a flared train. 
2 CONT Filmy tulle fell in gracely folds from a halo caught with large sprays of orange blossom.  She carried an exquisite bouquet of Frau Japane magnolias and sweet peas, which, together with all the other flowers were obtained from Syd
2 CONC ney and were the gift of Miss L Carruthers, of East Malvern (cousin of the bride).  The magnolias were similar to those which Miss Elaine Brookes carried on her wedding day.
2 CONT The church was decorated in pink and white phlox.
2 CONT The bride was attended by Miss Eileen Thornton of Sunshine, who was a charming maid in a frock of pretty pink crepe romaine, fitting the figure snugly and edged with frills. She wore a large hat the same shade as the frock, and he
2 CONC r posy comprised pin carnations, roses and sweet peas.
2 CONT Little Roma Huxtable, niece of the bridegroom, made a sweet little trainbearer in a frock of pink romaine edged with frills.  She carried a basket of pink carnations, roses and sweet peas.
2 CONT Mr E Hill acted as best man and carried out his duties in a capable manner. 
2 CONT Mrs Murray, mother of the bride, wore a frock of brown marocain, with cape and hat to match.  She carried a posy of autumn-tinted pansies and gladioli.  Mrs Kittelty, mother of the bridegroom, wore a navy blue frock, with swagger 
2 CONC coat. 
2 CONT Red carnations formed her posy. 
2 CONT Mr Sainty, of New Zealand, rendered a solo. "Because".
2 CONT After the ceremony a wedding breakfast was held at the home of the bridegroom's parents.  It was attended only by relatives and a few close friends. 
