1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Cairns James 1931 Reference AD960/1/55 Page 772 Will no 18584 
2 CONT
2 CONT Personal representatives of the said deceased was granted to the aforsaid Court to Ernest Linden Cairns and Harry Thomas Cairns both of Cairns Bay in Tasmania, Orchardists the executors named in the said Will
2 CONT
2 CONT I give devise and bequeath all my property whatsoever kind and nature and wheresoever situate to all my children who shall be living at my decease in equal shares as tenants in common.
2 CONT
2 CONT And in exercise of the power for this purpose given to me by the Will of John Hilton Dean dated the third day of August One thousand nine hundred and twelve and proved in the Supreme Court of Tasmania on the tenth day of September
2 CONC  One thousand nine hundred and twelve and of every other power enabling me in this behalf I devise and appoint the property therein referred to situate at Cairns Bay aforsaid containing Thirty three acres or thereabouts to my sons
2 CONC  the said Ernest Linden Cairns and Harry Thomas Cairns in equal shares as tenants in common absolutely.
