1 NAME Stanley Victor /Magee/
2 GIVN Stanley Victor
2 SURN Magee
2 _MARNM Magee
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 23 MAY 1891
2 PLAC Ballarat East, Vic
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 21 MAR 1934
2 PLAC Reefton Nz
2 ADDR
1 OCCU Hotelkeeper in Reefton
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth Cert no 19275 Stanley Victor McGee son of Minnie Dalton & James McGee
2 CONT
2 CONT Newspaper Cutout
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary 
2 CONT
2 CONT (Died 23.3.1934, written in pen)
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr Stanley V Magee
2 CONT
2 CONT The death took place at Reefton Hospital shortly before mid-day
2 CONT
2 CONT to-day of Mr Stanley Victor Magee, proprietor of the Buck's Head Hotel, Broadway, after a brief illness, and the occurrence has caused quite a gloom over the district, where he was one of the most popular residents.
2 CONT
2 CONT The deceased had not been in the best of health for some time past and about a fortnight ago took to his bed, and no improvement taking place he was removed to the Reefton Hospital on Sunday afternoon last, where he gradually grew
2 CONC  worse, until dissolution took place as stated this morning.
2 CONT
2 CONT The late Mr Magee was a very popular member of the Reefton Bowling Club, as well as a remarkably good player.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was also a member of Reefton Jockey and Trotting Clubs as well as other sporting bodies, and an ex-member of the Reefton Fire Brigade.
2 CONT
2 CONT Before taking over the Buck's Head Hotel Mr Magee was engaged in quartz mining at the Progress mine for some years, and later was coal mining at Bourke's Creek.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is survived by a widow and one son and one daughter, as well as his father and mother, Mr and Mrs James Magee, Sinnamon Street, two brothers, (Messrs Percy Magee, Auckland; and Alfred Magee, Waiuta) and three sisters (Mesdames 
2 CONC Sharpe and Jones, Auckland and Collis, Reefton). 
2 CONT
2 CONT The deceased was a native of Ballarat and 43 years of age. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He arrived in New Zealand with his parents in 1907
2 CONT
2 CONT and has resided in Reefton ever since, and the deepest sympathy will be extended to Mrs Magee, family and relatives in the sudden bereavement.
2 CONT
2 CONT The interment will take place on Friday afternoon, the funeral leaving his late residence, Broadway, at 1.40 o'clock for St Stephen's Church thenece to the Suburban Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
