1 NOTE {geni:about_me} On 28th July 1913 Myrtle gave birth to her twin daughters Zena and Edna.
2 CONT
2 CONT Myrtle gave  Zena to a neighbour to look after.  The neighbour's names were Beatrice and Frederick Haas.  Mr & Mrs. Haas adopted Zena and she became Zena Sharp-Haas - a name that was a combination of her biological name (Sharp) an
2 CONC d her adoptive parents' name.  Shortly afterwards, the Haas family moved back to Australia.  It was just a few months before World War I began.   The families lost all contact.
