1 NAME Alice W /Walker/
2 GIVN Alice W
2 SURN Walker
2 _MARNM Rebmann
1 SEX F
1 BURI
2 PLAC Park Hill Cemetery & Mausoleum
2 ADDR
3 CITY Bloomington
3 STAE Illinois
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 15 SEP 1907
2 ADDR
3 CITY Bloomington
3 STAE Illinois
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 30 AUG 2007
2 ADDR
3 CITY Bloomington
3 STAE Illinois
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} BLOOMINGTON - Alice Walker Rebmann, 99, of Bloomington, died 11:46 p.m. Thursday (Aug. 30, 2007) at OSF St. Joseph Medical Center, Bloomington.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her funeral will be at 11:30 a.m. Tuesday at Calvert & Metzler Memorial Home, Bloomington, with Pastor Thomas C. Wirsing officiating. Burial will be at Park Hill Cemetery, Bloomington. Visitation will be from 4 to 6 p.m. Monday at
2 CONC  the memorial home. Memorial gifts may be made to the Susan G. Komen Breast Cancer Foundation.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Rebmann was born Sept. 25, 1907, in Bloomington, a daughter of Samuel and Elizabeth Radley Walker. She married Clarence Rebmann on Aug. 12, 1932, at Bloomington. He died Sept. 10, 1965.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by two sons, Robert (Virginia) Rebmann, Tucson, Ariz., and Ronald (Marilyn) Rebmann, Bloomington; and a daughter, Jane (William) Smith, Bloomington; 11 grandchildren; 27 great-grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Rebmann was preceded in death by her parents, three sisters and one brother.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a member of Trinity Lutheran Church, Bloomington.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Rebmann had worked in sales for Livingston's and Klemm's department stores in downtown Bloomington prior to retirement.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a loving mother, grandmother and great grandmother who lived life to its fullest.
