1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jacob Gutmann died at age 25 after his schooner “Active” sunk near Victoria, British Columbia as a result of a gale.  He had been engaged in the seal fur trade in Victoria, along with his partner, Alexander Frank. 
2 CONC  The schooner, built in 1885, had been co–owned by the two partners.  In 1879, Jacob and his older brother David Gutmann worked for the Enterprise Mining Company in Victoria.   In  1880-1881, Jacob was partnered in a San Francisco
2 CONC  business with his brother David.  In the 1881 Canada Census, 19 year old Jacob is listed as a merchant living in Victoria in the household of George and Mary Ann Mason (both born in England). On October 22, 1888,  Jacob’s younger
2 CONC  brother Moritz Gutmann turned 21 and became Jacob’s sole heir in British Columbia.
