1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Addis GUTMANN, Jr.  Born in Seattle, 1930, a lifetime resident. He attended Laurelhurst Grade School and graduated from Lakeside and the University of Washington. In addition to his extended family and diverse circ
2 CONC le of friends, Addis loved baseball, the Huskies, food and cooking, working with young people, travel, Seattle and Laurelhurst. Addis served on the Boards of the University YMCA, The Burke Gilman Trail, The Educational Opportunity
2 CONC  Program at the University of Washington and NARAL Pro-Choice Washington. He was advisor to the University of Washington's Circle K Organization, served as past president of the NE Kiwanis and Temple De Hirsch Sinai. He coached Po
2 CONC ny League Baseball for 25 years and in 2005 was nominated for the Jefferson Award for public service. Survived by his wife, Leatrice; daughter and son-in-law, Wendy Gutmann and Jeff Menashe of Portland, Oregon; daughter and son-in
2 CONC -law, Lisa and Gary Kotzen of Seattle, Washington; daughter and son-in-law, Carolyn and Dean Roberts of Bremerton, Washington; and four granddaughters, Adina and Chantal Menashe, Hannah and Leila Kotzen. Funeral Services were held
2 CONC  at: Temple De Hirsch Sinai on Tuesday, September 5th with Internment at The Sephardic Brotherhood Cemetery. In lieu of flowers remembrances may be made to: NARAL Pro- Choice Washington or Kline Galland Home. Published in The Seat
2 CONC tle Times on Sept. 6, 2006 
