1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Oregonian, The (Portland, OR) - August 6, 1993
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral for Betty Rebecca Schneiderman of Southwest Portland will be at 1:30 p.m. Friday in the Weinstein Chapel of Neveh Zedek Cemetery. Burial will be in Rose City Lodge Cemetery .
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Schneiderman died of complications from diabetes Wednesday in a Portland hospital. She was 74.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born June 19, 1919, in Portland and was a lifelong resident of the city. Her maiden name was Posner. Mrs. Schneiderman had worked as a cosmetics and clothing sales clerk for Meier & Frank Co. and the old Ungar's store. She
2 CONC  had been actively involved with the Robison Jewish Home.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include her son, Martin of Portland; brother, Samuel Posner of Portland; and three granddaughters.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family suggests remembrances be contributions to Robison Jewish Home or to the Diabetes Association of Oregon.
