1 NAME Sally Joy /Krueger/
2 GIVN Sally Joy
2 SURN Krueger
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1 SEP 1926
2 PLAC Chicago, Cook, Illinois, United States
2 ADDR
3 STAE Illinois
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 8 FEB 2021
2 PLAC Northbrook, Cook, Illinois, United States
2 ADDR
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sally Krueger, most recently of Northbrook, IL, passed peacefully of natural causes on Feb. 8 at age 94. Born in Chicago, most of her youth was spent in New Jersey. Professionally, she distinguished herself as a co
2 CONC pywriter and creative director at a number of prominent advertising agencies in New York and Philadelphia. An avid reader, her interests included international travel, classical music, and fine art. She is survived by two nephews,
2 CONC  Tom Finger of Cedar Grove, NJ, and Jim Finger of Winnetka, IL, as well as a niece-in-law, Mandy Finger, who has been the family member most responsible for facilitating Sally's relocation to Illinois in 2000, as well as being the
2 CONC  individual most responsible for assuring Sally's senior years were among the happiest of her life. Other family members close to Sally were grandnieces Dee Bayro-Canady (and her sons Aidan and Dylan), Melinda Nowak (along with he
2 CONC r husband Jim; daughter Madison and son Nathan) and Emily Finger.
2 CONT
2 CONT Published by Chicago Tribune on Feb. 16, 2021.
2 CONT
